@startuml "Adapter - Telemetry (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Adapter — homework 3, the pluggable form


interface CelsiusSensor <<Target>> {
  + name() : String
  + readCelsius() : double
}

class FahrenheitProbe <<Adaptee>> {
  + getLabel() : String
  + currentF() : double
}

class KelvinThermometer <<Adaptee>> {
  + serial() : String
  + kelvin() : double
}

class PluggableSensorAdapter <<Adapter>> {
  - nameFn : Supplier<String>
  - celsiusFn : DoubleSupplier
  + {static} of(probe) : CelsiusSensor
  + {static} of(thermometer) : CelsiusSensor
}

CelsiusSensor <|.. PluggableSensorAdapter
PluggableSensorAdapter ..> FahrenheitProbe : via a lambda
PluggableSensorAdapter ..> KelvinThermometer : via a lambda

note right of PluggableSensorAdapter
  <b>One</b> adapter class, any number of
  instruments — GoF technique (c),
  p. 143.

  The obvious design is one adapter
  per adaptee, and a new class every
  quarter.
end note

note as N1
  The trade: nothing names the adaptee
  any more, so the compiler cannot check
  that the right conversion was paired
  with the right instrument.
end note

@enduml
